## Why This Is Asked
This tests mastery of modern CSS techniques: container queries, grid/flex interplay, accessibility with keyboard navigation, CSS-only accordions, and motion preferences. It pushes beyond viewport-breakpoint thinking.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid with container-type/container queries
- Checkbox-based accordion (no JS)
- CSS transitions and staggered entrances
- prefers-reduced-motion and accessibility (focus-visible)
- CSS variables and theming

## Code Example
```javascript
/* Minimal sketch: container, grid, card, details panel toggle */
:root { --bg: #fff; --fg: #111; }
.container { container-type: inline-size; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
@container (min-width: 420px) { .container { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@container (min-width: 700px) { .container { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
.card { border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
.card .details { max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; transition: max-height .25s ease; }
.card > input:checked ~ .details { max-height: 200px; }
```

