## Why This Is Asked
This probes end-to-end frontend experience: offline resilience, real-time UX, and robust networking.

## Key Concepts
- Service workers: offline cache strategies (stale-while-revalidate, cache-first)
- Fetch: AbortController, timeouts, error handling
- WebSocket: reconnection backoff, heartbeats, message ordering
- DOM: batched updates, minimal reflows, event replay from queues
- Persistence: IndexedDB for state / cache

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: sw.js: cache API, handle fetch events
self.addEventListener('fetch', e => {
  const url = new URL(e.request.url);
  if (url.pathname.startsWith('/api/')) {
    e.respondWith(fetch(e.request).catch(() => caches.match(e.request)));
  } else {
    e.respondWith(caches.match(e.request).then(r => r || fetch(e.request)));
  }
});
```

